<title>USA: Bayer nitric acid plant to be built by LBS.</title>
<headline>Bayer nitric acid plant to be built by LBS.</headline>
<dateline>OKLAHOMA CITY, Okla. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>LSB Industries Inc on Tuesday said its El Dorado Nitrogen unit has entered into definitive agreements with Bayer Corp to build and operate a nitric acid plant at Bayer's Baytown, Texas, chemical complex.</p>
<p>Bayer Corp is a unit of Bayer AG.</p>
<p>The plant, with a rated capacity of 443,000 tons a year, will supply nitric acid to Bayer's polyurethane units under a long-term supply contract, a news release issued by LSB said.</p>
<p>Construction is expected to be completed in the fall of 1998.</p>
</text>
